From cd7c91238740e34fc89f3378ec9efd81dfd90eda Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 13:45:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 16/17] atbm6031: log routine events at debug level

Every atbm_printk went out at KERN_ERR whatever its class, and the
default mask let through scans, block-ack sessions, LMAC and power
management: about 9 lines a minute at error level on a quiet link.
Print each class at its level, ERR and WARN as such and the rest at
debug, default the mask to ERR and WARN (atbm_printk_mask takes the
rest), and move routine events the driver logged as errors or
unconditionally to their class: scans, the SAE and 4-way handshake
steps, association, the probe's chip and firmware chatter.
atbm_printk_always prints at info level, as do latch_fwlog's firmware
lines, whatever the mask. The rekey setup no longer logs bytes of the
KEK and KCK.
